<title>UK: Next leads retailers higher after results.</title>
<headline>Next leads retailers higher after results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in leading UK retail groups rose on Wednesday as Next Plc romped higher after reporting profits at the top end of expectations coupled with a positive trading statement, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The Next results show that the leading stores groups are doing pretty well,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>Next shares were up 22-1/2p or 3.8 percent at 618-1/2 by 0856 GMT, the biggest gainer in the FTSE 100 index, pushing towards its record 639p set March 13, in volume of 1.1 million shares.</p>
</text>
